          "statement": "For a finite skeletal filtration, the AHSS edge morphisms are the stable structural maps between the abutment filtration stages and the surviving extreme-column subquotients induced by the D-to-E and E-to-D maps of the exact couple. This description uses boundedness in the skeletal index p and does not assume that the coefficient index q is bounded or first-quadrant.",
