          "id": "lem-pairings-of-skeletal-exact-couples-induce-multiplicative-ahss",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "proof_plan": "Pair the relative groups of skeletal pairs by the external product, the collapse to the (p,r) block of the product filtration quotient, and pullback along the cellular diagonal, giving a typed bilinear mu_1: E_1^{p,q} x E_1^{r,s} -> E_1^{p+r,q+s} together with the corresponding pairing of the relative D-terms; naturality of the external product makes the restriction, connecting and pair maps multiplicative. The two relative connecting-map Leibniz identities give d_1 mu_1(x,y) = mu_1(d_1x,y) + (-1)^{p+q} mu_1(x,d_1y) for d_1 = jk, so mu_1 carries cycles to cycles and sends B x Z + Z x B to boundaries and descends to a pairing mu_2 on E_2 = H(E_1,d_1). Forgetting support gives F^p F^q contained in F^{p+q}, and finite convergence identifies the stable product with the associated-graded product. Only the ring products from E_2 on, their derivations and the ring isomorphism E_{r+1} = H(E_r,d_r) are taken from the standard multiplicative structure of a pairing of filtering towers; step 7.2 records an explicit six-segment cellular diagonal of the interval whose first-page pairing is not associative, so no E_1 ring is asserted.",
