                "url": "https://pages.uoregon.edu/ddugger/multb.pdf"
              },
              {
                "locator": "Lecture 29, product structure, printed pp. 100–101",
                "title": "Miller, MIT 18.906 Algebraic Topology II",
                "url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-906-algebraic-topology-ii-spring-2020/e8a061a73ca1a451df8809c7a7fbc846_MIT18_906S20_notes.pdf"
              },
              {
                "locator": "§1.3, printed p. 4: the AHSS as stated carries no information about multiplicative structure",
                "title": "Ji, The Atiyah–Hirzebruch Spectral Sequence",
                "url": "https://www.math.columbia.edu/~calebji/atiyah-hirzebruch-final.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let h be a reduced generalized cohomology theory with a coherent external product (unital, associative, graded-commutative, compatible with suspension, with the two relative connecting-map Leibniz identities). For a finite CW complex with skeleta X^p and a cellular approximation of the diagonal: the relative products of skeletal pairs, the collapse to the (p,r) block and the diagonal give a typed bilinear pairing mu_1: E_1^{p,q} x E_1^{r,s} -> E_1^{p+r,q+s} with E_1^{p,q}=h^{p+q}(X^p,X^{p-1}), and the same construction pairs h^m(X,X^{p-1}) with h^n(X,X^{r-1}) into h^{m+n}(X,X^{p+r-1}); mu_1 is natural for morphisms of theories and for cellular maps whose chosen filtered diagonals commute strictly, but no naturality is claimed for independently chosen diagonals, and it carries no associativity, graded commutativity or unitality in general. d_1 = jk satisfies the Leibniz rule with respect to mu_1, and mu_1 descends to a pairing mu_2 on E_2 = H(E_1,d_1); from E_2 on the products make every page a natural unital associative graded-commutative bigraded ring on which d_r is a derivation, with E_{r+1} = H(E_r,d_r) as bigraded rings and mu_2 the graded cup product under E_2^{p,q} = H^p(X;h^q(*)), so the product is independent of the diagonal from the second page on. The filtration is multiplicative, F^p F^q contained in F^{p+q}, and E_infinity = gr_F h^*(X) as graded rings.",
          "title": "Pairings of skeletal exact couples induce multiplicative AHSS"
        },
